# Normalize line endings so a clone behaves identically on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) checks text files
# out as CRLF. The round-trip fixtures are byte-significant markdown — a soft
# break is a lone LF — so a CRLF checkout fails nine tests in
# tests/roundtrip/ that pass everywhere else. Pinning the working tree to LF
# keeps the corpus meaningful and the test suite green on Windows too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated; collapse in review and keep out of language stats.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
docs/screenshots/* linguist-generated
